detective: In the end you've killed them both
detective: And how do you feel now, Mina?

mina: I thought about it, about Jose
mina: Her smile, her laugh and her voice

mina: I also thought about Ruby
mina: Her beauty, her confidence and her love for Josephine

mina: Finally I thought about myself...
mina: The ugly disgusting monster I had become

mina: ....empty
mina: I feel...empty

detective: And what about the love, the love you felt for her

mina: Is it love if you destroy what you love?, To kill the Goddess you once claimed to adore

detective: No, Mina. That is not love, that is obsession
detective: And obsession is just love that forgot to let go

nn: I cried for the first time in a long time, not for myself...
nn: For Ruby.....

nn: I cried for what could have been if I had confessed, If I had let go, If...I had been brave
nn: But it was to late, I was sentenced to 25 years in prison
nn: Now I am in a cell where I will never see the sun nor her again
nn: But sometimes before I sleep, when there is no noise and the lights are off
nn: I can see her face

nn: Josephine...
nn: My Josephine, my angel and my unfortunate victim
nn: I'm sorry, I'm truly sorry
nn: I loved you, I loved you more than anything and I still do
nn: But love is not enough
nn: It never was